{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","packSha":"ce51f8daf33a7ad1f1bb6a1322498cffea1b60ef3fb09cc7f780363d297456b5","packTokens":1956,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":67,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":357,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":705,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":757,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":8,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"Map each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"When an invoice is 7 days past its due date, the system shall mark it overdue and show it on the overdue list\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"When staff press 'Send reminder' on an overdue invoice, the system shall email the customer a reminder with the invoice number, amount and due date\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"The system shall record each reminder sent, with who sent it and when, and show the history on the invoice\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"If an email cannot be delivered, the system shall show the failure on the invoice and keep it on the overdue list\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Staff shall be able to filter the overdue list by customer and by days overdue\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-6\",\n  \"text\": \"Build overdue list screen (table, filters, a 'Send reminder' button per row)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-7\",\n  \"text\": \"Build invoice detail screen (amount, due date, reminder history, delivery failures)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"Who can view the screens and send reminders, and how do staff sign in?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Any authenticated staff user, using the existing API's authentication\",\n  \"by\": \"mhamza\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"Which email address receives the reminder, and what happens if the customer has several contacts or none?\",\n  \"answer\": \"The customer's single billing email from the existing record; if missing, the send is blocked with an error\",\n  \"by\": \"mhamza\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"Can reminder history entries be edited or deleted?\",\n  \"answer\": \"No, they are append-only and immutable\",\n  \"by\": \"mhamza\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"Payments are out of scope. So how does an invoice come off the overdue list once it is paid or closed?\",\n  \"answer\": \"The existing system's invoice status (paid/cancelled) is read and closed invoices drop off automatically\",\n  \"by\": \"mhamza\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"How should repeated sends be guarded against?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Disable the button while a send is in progress only\",\n  \"by\": \"mhamza\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"Is 'overdue' a status saved on the invoice (for example by a daily job), or is it worked out from the due date each time the list loads?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Computed at query time from due date and today's date\",\n  \"by\": \"mhamza\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"Where are reminder history records stored, given that invoices live in the client's existing system?\",\n  \"answer\": \"New table in the same Postgres database, referencing invoice ID\",\n  \"by\": \"mhamza\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"Is a failed send recorded in the append-only reminder history, and does a later successful send clear the failure shown on the invoice?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Every attempt (success or failure) is a history entry; the latest status is shown\",\n  \"by\": \"mhamza\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"The system shall determine, on every request rather than by storing a flag, whether an invoice is overdue.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"An invoice shall be considered overdue only if its status is in a configured list of open statuses, which defaults to just 'open'.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"An invoice shall be considered overdue only if it has a due date.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"An invoice shall be considered overdue only if the number of calendar days from its due date to today, calculated in a configured business time zone, is at least a configured overdue threshold, which defaults to 7.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"The system shall provide an authenticated staff endpoint that returns the list of all invoices currently classified as overdue.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Each invoice in the overdue list shall include its invoice ID, invoice number, customer name, amount, due date, and days overdue, where days overdue is the calendar days since the due date.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"The overdue list endpoint shall support filtering results by a customer identifier, returning only that customer's overdue invoices.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"The overdue list endpoint shall support filtering results by a days-overdue bucket, using fixed inclusive ranges of 7-30, 31-60, and 61+ days, regardless of the configured overdue threshold.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"If the requested bucket value is not one of the three defined buckets, the endpoint shall respond with HTTP 400 and a validation error identifying the bucket parameter.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Any request to an Invoice Reminders endpoint without valid staff authentication shall be rejected with HTTP 401, without returning invoice data, sending email, or changing data.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Any request to an Invoice Reminders endpoint with a valid, unexpired token whose principal is not a staff user shall be rejected with HTTP 403, without returning invoice or customer data or changing data.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}